From: =?UTF-8?q?Lajosh=C3=A1zi=2C=20L=C3=A1szl=C3=B3=20Gergely?= <lajoshazilg@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 17:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] camera: make the focus mode and its slider actually arrive

Three faults, one cause: the focus mode is chosen long before there is a
camera to tell.

The mode is read from the setting while the window is built, and written
to the camera as a PipeWire property - which only exists once the node is
configured. A write before that goes nowhere and reports nothing, so the
camera stayed in its own default, continuous hunting, while the menu
showed the mode the user had picked. Re-applying at Ready helped but did
not settle it: the node can be there with its controls not yet
published. Since nothing can be read back to check, keep asking until
the controls are there to be written, a few times a second for ten
seconds, and say so in the log if they never turn up.

The distance slider had the same lateness with a worse ending: it is
built from the lens's own bounds, so with no camera to ask there was no
slider, and the popover was built once at start-up and never again. The
slider was therefore missing for good, including in Off where it is the
only thing that moves the lens. Build the popover again when the camera
is up, and only while the slider is still missing, so that a later Ready
does not shut a popover the user has open.

Signed-off-by: Lajosházi, László Gergely <lajoshazilg@gmail.com>
Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
